Imports:
  - Types:
      - Track
    From: domain/src/main/java/tachiyomi/domain/track/model
  - Types:
      - TrackRepository
    From: domain/src/main/java/tachiyomi/domain/track/repository

Usages:
  sqldelight_row_mapper: |
    SqlDelight generates one query method per SQL statement, each accepting a mapper lambda
    that receives the row's columns as individual typed parameters and returns the target domain
    type. A mapper object groups these lambdas as top-level functions so query call sites can
    pass e.g. TrackMapper::mapTrack directly.

Annotations: |
  This cell is the concrete, SqlDelight-backed implementation of `TrackRepository`, the
  structural counterpart of data/manga for the track aggregate.

  Use `Track`/`TrackRepository` from Imports throughout.
  Use `sqldelight_row_mapper` for how rows become domain objects.

---

"TrackRepository::TrackRepositoryImpl(database: Database)":
  location: TrackRepositoryImpl.kt
  annotations: |
    Implements every `TrackRepository` method against SqlDelight-generated queries on
    `database`, mapping rows through `TrackMapper`.

    `database`: the app's SqlDelight Database handle

    Algorithm:
    1. Read methods run a generated query with TrackMapper::mapTrack as row mapper
    2. insert/insertAll share one private insertValues(vararg tracks) helper that writes
       every row inside database.transaction, so bulk inserts commit atomically

    Use `sqldelight_row_mapper`.

"TrackMapper()":
  location: TrackMapper.kt
  annotations: |
    Stateless SqlDelight row-to-domain-object mapping function consumed by
    `TrackRepositoryImpl`.

    Use `sqldelight_row_mapper`.
  methods:
    "mapTrack(id: Long, mangaId: Long, syncId: Long, remoteId: Long, title: String, status: Long, score: Double) -> track:Track": |
      Build a `Track` from one manga_sync table row plus its remaining scalar columns
      (libraryId, lastChapterRead, totalChapters, remoteUrl, startDate, finishDate, private, not
      individually listed here for brevity). Note the column is named `syncId` in SQL but maps
      to Track.trackerId.

